{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Gs8TSLTo3xze4jDmsJ6qoh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for every \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier definition. Each prediction needs a result_rationale explaining why we'd get that result under the best-case scenario.\n\nLet me go through all planned experiments:\n\n1. plan_008 (exp_008e_v2) - PREPARING status, but there's exp_008e_v3 RUNNING with some data\n2. plan_010 - Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2 - planned\n3. plan_011 - Walker Walk 008d seeds 1-2 - planned\n\n\n4. plan_012 - Walker Walk 008f seeds 1-2 - planned\n5. plan_013 - Walker Walk 008a seeds 1-2 - planned\n6. plan_020 - Cheetah Run baseline 3 seeds - planned\n7. plan_021 - Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON 3 seeds - planned\n8. plan_022 - Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON 3 seeds - planned\n9. plan_023 - Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample 3 seeds - planned\n10. plan_030 - continuing through the rest of the planned experiments including RSSM prediction quality, actor entropy analysis, value prediction distribution, dt_embedding cosine similarity, and Hopper Hop validation.\n\nRight now plan_007 is running with partial results while plan_008 is preparing, though plan_008e_v3 is already executing. I should focus on the experiments marked as planned or preparing that still need conclusive data. The causal chain for the best tier is solid—dt_embedding is the root cause, Cheetah Run confirms the mechanism, and multi-seed consistency looks strong. For plan_008 specifically, I'm expecting subsample ON with untrained dt_emb at H=15 to show particular behavior patterns.\n\nLooking at plan_008e_v3, it's already showing 382.2 at 45K steps (86% of baseline) with a normalized value-to-error ratio of 0.876x, which suggests untrained dt_emb provides protection even when subsampling is enabled. I'd expect the eval return to climb into the 700-800 range by 105K steps, similar to what plan_008a achieved, while keeping that normalized ratio below 1.0x throughout. For plan_010 with Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2, the best tier shows seeds reproducing near the original asymptotic performance around 950 with value-to-error stabilizing in the 69-72% range. Plan_011 testing Walker Walk with the 008d variant on seeds 1-2 should replicate the collapse pattern seen across all 3 seeds in the best tier, with normalized ratios exceeding 1.5x and eval returns peaking early before declining. Plan_012 is examining Walker Walk with the 008f variant.\n\nCompleting that thought: all 3 seeds remain stable with normalized ratios consistently below 1.0x. Plan_013 runs Walker Walk with the 008a variant on seeds 1-2, and the V-recovery pattern should replicate with mean returns in the 700-850 range by 105K steps. Now shifting to Cheetah Run experiments—plan_020 establishes the baseline across 3 seeds, and I'm estimating DreamerV3 typically reaches around 800-900 on Cheetah Run, so I'll use 850 as the asymptotic target. Plan_021 tests the trained dt_emb variant, which should trigger the same delusional critic mechanism with normalized ratios above 1.5x leading to collapse. Plan_022 with dt_embed_dim=0 should stay stable with ratios below 1.0x, while plan_023 using untrained dt_emb should show the V-recovery pattern with returns in the 70-90 range.\n\nNow I'm looking at the diagnostic metrics across these configurations. Plan_030 examines RSSM prediction quality and should show a clear fidelity gap between dt=2 and dt=1 timesteps. Plan_031 tracks actor entropy, where collapsed configs should exhibit increased entropy. Plan_032 analyzes value prediction distributions, with trained dt_emb showing right-skewed overestimation. Plan_033 measures dt_embedding cosine similarity, expecting divergence between dt=1 and dt=2 embeddings during training. Plan_040 replicates the same pattern in Hopper Hop as a third environment test. I'm about to write out the full YAML with detailed predictions and metrics, using around 800 as the Cheetah Run baseline estimate.\n\nNow I'm reviewing the specific metric ranges for the best tier across these experiments—looking at normalized value estimation scores, eval returns, replication counts across seeds, peak performance with and without dt embeddings, performance ratios, and the number of claims supported by strong evidence.\n\nFor plan_007 with the 008f variant, I see it's already running with data collected up to 35K steps, so I need to extrapolate what the metrics should look like when it reaches 55K based on the expected ranges in the best tier.\n\nLet me work through the YAML predictions systematically for each experiment.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20446,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20446},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bef9a362-8ebf-4bcb-9f30-9fef8cba03ac","uuid":"d9faf75c-f540-4506-ac69-8232a45dabd2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Gs8TSLTo3xze4jDmsJ6qoh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  完整因果诊断论文。标题 \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails\"。\n  核心因果链：trained dt_embedding → RSSM fidelity gap → delusional critic → collapse，\n  经 factorial ablation + 双环境 + 多种子三重验证闭合。\n  v/e overshoot ratio >1.5x 作为可复用诊断工具。C2 升级为 confirmed。\n  Discussion 明确建议：不要在当前 RSSM 架构中联合训练 dt_embedding。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: 008f 继续运行至 55K（已有 35K 数据）\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk dt_embed_dim=0 H=8 — 55K completion\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      008f 已运行至 35K，继续至 55K+ 确认 normalized v/e 持续收敛，\n      eval 稳定在 190-260 范围，与 008d 的 diverging pattern 形成完整对照。\n    expected_results:\n      eval_return_45K: 215\n      eval_return_55K: 230\n      eval_return_65K: 238\n      value_mean_45K: 55.0\n      value_mean_55K: 76.0\n      value_eval_ratio_45K: 0.256\n      value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.330\n      normalized_ve_45K: 0.77\n      normalized_ve_55K: 0.82\n      normalized_ve_65K: 0.72\n      vs_baseline_55K: \"-63.2%\"\n      collapse: false\n      gate_dt_mean: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      dt_embed_dim=0 意味着 critic 在 imagination 中无法获得 dt 信息，\n      因此无法对 dt=2 步骤做出 dt-specific 的价值估计。\n      RSSM 仍然用 dt=2 transition 训练（subsample ON），所以 world model \n      对 dt=2 dynamics 的预测质量仍然有限，限制了绝对性能（~230 vs baseline 950）。\n      但关键是：没有 dt_embedding → critic 不会因 dt-conditioned \n      overestimation 而 diverge。v/e 应跟随或略低于 baseline 的自然增长曲线\n      （normalized ~0.7-0.85x），绝不会出现 008d 那种 >1.5x 的 pathological \n      overshoot。45K→55K 的 normalized v/e 从 0.77→0.82 是自然漂移，\n      不是 accelerating divergence。这直接证明 dt_embedding conditioning \n      （而非 RSSM 的 dt=2 dynamics 本身）是 delusional critic 的 root cause。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008f vs 008d — Causal Isolation\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Metric\", \"008f (no dt_emb)\", \"008d (trained dt_emb)\", \"Interpretation\"]\n          - [\"normalized_ve_25K\", \"1.02x\", \"1.78x\", \"008d 已进入 pathological\"]\n          - [\"normalized_ve_35K\", \"0.73x\", \"1.71x\", \"008f 收敛，008d 持续 diverge\"]\n          - [\"normalized_ve_45K\", \"0.77x (pred)\", \"2.09x\", \"gap 扩大至 2.7x 差异\"]\n          - [\"normalized_ve_55K\", \"0.82x (pred)\", \"— (已 collapse)\", \"008f 稳定\"]\n          - [\"eval_return_45K\", \"~215 (pred)\", \"140.8\", \"008f 略高，无 collapse\"]\n          - [\"collapse\", \"No\", \"Yes (@35K)\", \"单变量隔离确认\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"双 Y 轴图：左轴 normalized v/e ratio，右轴 eval return。008f（蓝，实线）和 008d（红，虚线）并排。008d 的 v/e 从 1.78x→2.09x 加速上升同时 eval 下降形成 'X 交叉'；008f 的 v/e 在 0.7-0.85x 水平波动，eval 缓慢上升。灰色水平线标注 1.5x pathological threshold。\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是整篇论文的 smoking gun。008f 与 008d 仅差一个变量：dt_embedding。\n      008d 有 trained dt_embedding → normalized v/e 1.78x→2.09x → collapse；\n      008f 无 dt_embedding → normalized v/e 0.73x→0.82x → stable。\n      因果归因闭合：dt_embedding conditioning 是 delusional critic 的充要条件。\n      RSSM 的 dt=2 prediction quality 本身不足以触发 collapse（008f 证明），\n      但给 critic 提供 dt 信息后，critic 会 exploit 这些不准确的 dt-conditioned \n      predictions 来系统性高估 value。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: 008e_v2 — untrained dt_emb + subsample ON + H=15\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk untrained dt_emb + subsample ON H=15\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      解耦 008a 的 B+ protection 来源：是 untrained dt_emb 还是 subsample OFF？\n      008e_v3 已在运行（45K 数据：382.2, v/e=0.876x），预测完整轨迹。\n    expected_results:\n      eval_return_45K: 382\n      eval_return_55K: 430\n      eval_return_65K: 490\n      eval_return_75K: 460\n      eval_return_85K: 520\n      eval_return_95K: 550\n      eval_return_105K: 640\n      value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.36\n      value_eval_ratio_65K: 0.40\n      value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.45\n      normalized_ve_45K: 0.88\n      normalized_ve_55K: 0.89\n      normalized_ve_65K: 0.71\n      normalized_ve_105K: 0.69\n      vs_baseline_105K: \"-30.1%\"\n      collapse: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      untrained dt_emb + subsample ON + H=15 结合了两个效应：\n      (1) untrained dt_emb 阻止 dt-conditioned value overestimation（同 008a 机制），\n      (2) subsample ON 减少有效训练 transition 数量，比 008a（subsample OFF）学得慢。\n      因此绝对性能低于 008a（640 vs 778 @105K），但同样不会 collapse。\n      normalized v/e 保持 <1.0x 证明 protection 来自 untrained dt_emb（而非 subsample OFF），\n      因为 subsample ON 的训练数据分布与 008d 相同，唯一差异是 dt_emb 是否 trained。\n      相比 008a 的两次 V-recovery，这里预期振荡幅度更小（subsample ON \n      → 更稳定但更慢的学习信号），呈现缓慢单调上升而非剧烈 V 形。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"B+ Protection 归因：008a vs 008e_v2 vs 008d\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Config\", \"subsample\", \"dt_emb\", \"eval@105K\", \"norm_ve@105K\", \"collapse\"]\n          - [\"008a\", \"OFF\", \"untrained\", \"778\", \"0.59x\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"008e_v2 (pred)\", \"ON\", \"untrained\", \"~640\", \"~0.69x\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"008d\", \"ON\", \"trained\", \"— (collapse@35K)\", \"2.09x@45K\", \"Yes\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三条学习曲线叠加：008a（蓝）显示 V-recovery 到 778，008e_v2（绿）显示较慢但稳定的上升到 ~640，008d（红）显示 35K 后 collapse。下方子图显示 normalized v/e，008a 和 008e_v2 均在 1.0x 以下，008d 在 1.5x 以上。\"\n    analysis: >\n      008e_v2 是 C3/C5 的关键解耦实验。如果 008a 的 protection 来自 subsample OFF\n      （更多训练数据），那么 008e_v2（subsample ON）应该 collapse。\n      但 008e_v2 不 collapse 且 normalized v/e <1.0x，证明 protection \n      的主因是 untrained dt_emb，subsample 只影响收敛速度。\n      这也强化了 C5：learning signal reduction 是 secondary factor，不是 root cause。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_010: Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      2 个额外 seed 建立 baseline v/e 校准的置信区间，\n      为 008d/008f 多种子 normalized v/e 计算提供 per-seed reference。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_last10_mean: 940\n      seed2_eval_return_last10_mean: 960\n      three_seed_mean: 950.3\n      three_seed_std: 9.5\n      seed1_ve_35K: 0.23\n      seed2_ve_35K: 0.25\n      seed1_ve_55K: 0.39\n      seed2_ve_55K: 0.42\n      seed1_ve_105K: 0.64\n      seed2_ve_105K: 0.68\n      ve_35K_mean: 0.240\n      ve_35K_std: 0.013\n      ve_55K_mean: 0.405\n      ve_55K_std: 0.015\n      ve_105K_mean: 0.660\n      ve_105K_std: 0.014\n      ve_stable_range: \"68-73%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker Walk 是 DMC 中最稳定的环境之一，DreamerV3 baseline 的 seed 间方差极小。\n      seed 0 的 asymptotic 950.9 ± ~10 是典型值。v/e ratio 的 seed 间方差\n      主要来自 eval return 的随机波动（±15-20），而 value function 的收敛轨迹\n      高度一致（因为 world model 在此简单环境中很快收敛）。\n      三种子均值 ~950、std <10 为后续所有 normalized v/e 计算提供了\n      robust 的 per-step reference curve，使得 \"1.5x = pathological\" \n      的 threshold 具有统计意义（而非单种子巧合）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Baseline v/e Calibration (3 seeds)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Step\", \"Seed 0\", \"Seed 1 (pred)\", \"Seed 2 (pred)\", \"Mean±Std\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"0.241\", \"0.23\", \"0.25\", \"0.240±0.013\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"0.404\", \"0.39\", \"0.42\", \"0.405±0.015\"]\n          - [\"105K\", \"0.656\", \"0.64\", \"0.68\", \"0.660±0.014\"]\n          - [\"Asymptotic\", \"~70%\", \"~69%\", \"~72%\", \"~70±1.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"v/e ratio vs training step 带 shaded confidence band（3 seeds）。中线为均值，shaded region 为 ±1 std。水平虚线标注 asymptotic ~70%。此图作为后续所有 normalized v/e 计算的 reference。\"\n    analysis: >\n      baseline 多种子的意义不在于确认 Walker Walk 能解决（这是 trivial 的），\n      而在于建立 v/e ratio 的 per-step reference distribution。\n      单种子 normalized v/e 有 ±5-8% 的 noise，三种子均值将 noise 降到 ±3-4%，\n      使得 \"008d 的 1.7x 是 pathological\" 的判断从 \"很可能\" 升级为 \"统计显著\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_011: Walker Walk 008d seeds 1-2 (collapse replication)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      复现 delusional critic collapse：3/3 seeds 均应在 25K-45K \n      出现 normalized v/e >1.5x 并触发 eval return 持续下降。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_25K: 155\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 138\n      seed1_eval_return_45K: 125\n      seed2_eval_return_25K: 172\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 152\n      seed2_eval_return_45K: 133\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.62\n      seed1_normalized_ve_45K: 1.95\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.80\n      seed2_normalized_ve_45K: 2.15\n      three_seed_collapse_count: 3\n      three_seed_peak_return_mean: 165\n      three_seed_peak_return_std: 12\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_45K_mean: 2.06\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_45K_std: 0.13\n    result_rationale: >\n      trained dt_embedding 导致的 delusional critic 是结构性问题，不是随机事件。\n      机制：trained dt_emb 让 critic 在 imagination 中为 dt=2 步骤学到\n      dt-specific 的 value estimate，但 RSSM 在 dt=2 transition 上的\n      prediction fidelity 不足以支撑这种精度 → critic 系统性高估 → actor \n      追逐虚假梯度 → eval return 下降 → 正反馈循环。\n      这个机制对初始化不敏感（dt_embedding 的训练方向由 RSSM 的 dt=2 \n      prediction bias 决定，而该 bias 在不同 seed 中方向一致——都是 overestimate），\n      因此预期 3/3 seeds 全部 collapse，seed 间 normalized v/e 的方差很小（±0.13）。\n      collapse 的时间点可能有 ±5K step 的偏差，但模式完全一致。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008d Collapse Replication (3 seeds)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Metric\", \"Seed 0\", \"Seed 1 (pred)\", \"Seed 2 (pred)\", \"Consistency\"]\n          - [\"Peak eval return\", \"167@25K\", \"155@25K\", \"172@25K\", \"Mean 165±9\"]\n          - [\"Eval @45K\", \"140.8\", \"~125\", \"~133\", \"All declining\"]\n          - [\"Norm v/e @35K\", \"1.71x\", \"1.62x\", \"1.80x\", \"All >1.5x ✓\"]\n          - [\"Norm v/e @45K\", \"2.09x\", \"1.95x\", \"2.15x\", \"All >1.5x ✓\"]\n          - [\"Collapse?\", \"Yes\", \"Yes\", \"Yes\", \"3/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三条 eval return 曲线（红色系，不同 line style 区分 seed）全部呈 inverted-V 后持续下降。右侧子图显示 normalized v/e 全部 >1.5x（灰色 threshold 线以上）。配对标注 '3/3 seeds collapse'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      3/3 collapse 复现是 best tier 的 defining criterion 之一。\n      这将 C2 从 \"provisional\" 升级为 \"confirmed\"，因为 collapse 不是\n      单种子的随机异常，而是 trained dt_embedding 的必然结果。\n      reviewer R6 的 \"single seed\" concern 被直接消解。\n      seed 间一致性（normalized v/e std ~0.13）还表明 1.5x threshold \n      是 robust 的诊断标准，不需要 per-seed calibration。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_012: Walker Walk 008f seeds 1-2 (stability replication)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: >\n      复现 causal control 的稳定性：3/3 seeds 的 normalized v/e \n      持续 <1.0x，无 collapse，与 008d 形成完美对照。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 220\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 240\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 0.70\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.78\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 0.76\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.85\n      three_seed_eval_55K_mean: 232\n      three_seed_eval_55K_std: 16\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_55K_mean: 0.80\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_55K_std: 0.06\n      three_seed_stable_count: 3\n      collapse: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      dt_embed_dim=0 从架构上消除了 dt conditioning 通路。\n      无论 seed 如何变化，critic 都无法获得 dt 信息，因此无法形成\n      dt-specific 的 overestimation。这是架构级的保护，不依赖初始化。\n      性能低（~230 vs baseline 950）是因为 subsample ON 减少了训练数据\n      且 H=8 horizon 太短，但这与 collapse 是完全不同的 failure mode。\n      normalized v/e 在 0.7-0.85x 范围的 seed 间方差来自 eval return \n      的随机波动，不会突破 1.0x，更不会到 1.5x pathological zone。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008f vs 008d 多种子对照\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"\", \"008f norm_ve (3 seeds)\", \"008d norm_ve (3 seeds)\"]\n          - [\"@35K\", \"0.73, 0.70, 0.76\", \"1.71, 1.62, 1.80\"]\n          - [\"@55K\", \"0.82, 0.78, 0.85\", \"collapse, collapse, collapse\"]\n          - [\"Mean±Std @35K\", \"0.73±0.03\", \"1.71±0.09\"]\n          - [\"Collapse rate\", \"0/3\", \"3/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot 或 violin plot：x 轴为 config（008f vs 008d），y 轴为 normalized v/e @35K。008f 的分布完全在 1.0x 以下，008d 完全在 1.5x 以上，无重叠。1.5x threshold 水平线标注。\"\n    analysis: >\n      008f 3/3 stable + 008d 3/3 collapse = 完美的 6-point causal contrast。\n      effect size 极大（Cohen's d > 10），统计检验的 p-value 可以忽略。\n      这直接回答了论文的核心问题：为什么 temporal abstraction 失败？\n      答案：因为 trained dt_embedding 让 critic exploit RSSM 的 fidelity gap。\n      移除 dt_embedding → 移除 exploit 通路 → 消除 collapse。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_013: Walker Walk 008a seeds 1-2 (V-recovery replication)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: >\n      复现 value growth suppression 和 V-recovery pattern，\n      确认 untrained dt_emb 的保护效应跨 seed 一致。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_65K: 580\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 720\n      seed2_eval_return_65K: 630\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 810\n      three_seed_mean_105K: 769\n      three_seed_std_105K: 46\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.62\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.55\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_105K_mean: 0.59\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_105K_std: 0.04\n      v_recovery_count: \"3/3 show at least one V-recovery\"\n      collapse: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      untrained dt_emb 的 protection 机制是架构性的（random fixed embedding \n      阻断 dt-specific value learning），因此 V-recovery pattern 应跨 seed 复现。\n      但 V-recovery 的具体时间和幅度受 exploration noise 影响较大：\n      actor 在 random dt_embedding 下的梯度信号较弱且含噪，导致 policy \n      在局部最优间振荡（V 的下降段），然后通过 value function 的 slow \n      catch-up 恢复（V 的上升段）。seed 0 有两次 V-recovery，\n      其他 seed 可能只有一次或三次，但模式一致：振荡但不 collapse。\n      三种子均值 769±46 @105K 对应 baseline 的 84%（best tier 定义 700-850），\n      normalized v/e 均值 0.59±0.04 远低于 pathological threshold。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008a V-Recovery Replication (3 seeds)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Seed\", \"Peak@65K\", \"Dip (min after peak)\", \"@105K\", \"Norm v/e@105K\", \"V-recoveries\"]\n          - [\"Seed 0\", \"608\", \"470@75K\", \"778\", \"0.59x\", \"2\"]\n          - [\"Seed 1 (pred)\", \"580\", \"440@75K\", \"720\", \"0.62x\", \"1-2\"]\n          - [\"Seed 2 (pred)\", \"630\", \"490@85K\", \"810\", \"0.55x\", \"2\"]\n          - [\"Mean±Std\", \"606±25\", \"467±25\", \"769±46\", \"0.59±0.04\", \"All ≥1\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三条 eval return 曲线（蓝色系）叠加显示 V-recovery pattern，每条都有振荡但无 collapse。shaded band 显示 ±1 std。下方子图 normalized v/e 三条线全部在 1.0x 以下且随训练递减。\"\n    analysis: >\n      V-recovery 的多种子复现证明这是 untrained dt_emb 的系统性行为，\n      而非 seed 0 的巧合。振荡的存在表明 dt=2 imagination 仍然引入了\n      learning instability（vs baseline 的 smooth convergence），\n      但 untrained dt_emb 将 instability 的上界限制在 \"振荡\" 而非 \"collapse\"。\n      这支持 C3 的核心论点：untrained dt_emb substantively protects performance。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_020: Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: >\n      建立 Cheetah Run 的 dt=1 reference，包括 asymptotic return \n      和 v/e calibration curve，为跨环境泛化提供 second environment anchor。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_asymptotic: 810\n      seed1_eval_return_asymptotic: 790\n      seed2_eval_return_asymptotic: 830\n      three_seed_mean_asymptotic: 810\n      three_seed_std_asymptotic: 20\n      ve_35K_mean: 0.21\n      ve_55K_mean: 0.38\n      ve_105K_mean: 0.60\n      ve_stable_range: \"62-68%\"\n      fps: 7.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah Run 在 DreamerV3 中的典型 asymptotic return 为 780-850。\n      相比 Walker Walk（~950），Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更复杂\n      （连续前进、速度控制），但 RSSM 仍能有效建模 dt=1 transition。\n      v/e ratio 的增长曲线与 Walker Walk 类似但 asymptotic 略低（~65% vs ~70%），\n      因为 Cheetah Run 的 reward scale 和 episode structure 不同，\n      value function 的 calibration 稍有差异。\n      三种子方差 std ~20 略高于 Walker Walk（std ~10），因为 Cheetah Run \n      的探索空间更大，不同 seed 可能发现略不同的 gait pattern。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah Run Baseline v/e Calibration\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Step\", \"Mean v/e\", \"Std\", \"vs Walker baseline\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"0.21\", \"0.02\", \"Walker: 0.24 (similar)\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"0.38\", \"0.03\", \"Walker: 0.40 (similar)\"]\n          - [\"105K\", \"0.60\", \"0.03\", \"Walker: 0.66 (slightly lower)\"]\n          - [\"Asymptotic\", \"~65%\", \"~3%\", \"Walker: ~70%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Walker Walk vs Cheetah Run baseline v/e ratio 并排图，显示两个环境的 calibration curve 形状相似但量级略有差异，建立 cross-environment reference。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah Run baseline 的主要目的是为 normalized v/e 计算提供 \n      environment-specific reference。如果两环境的 v/e calibration curve \n      形状一致（都是 monotonic 增长到 asymptotic），则 1.5x threshold \n      可以 environment-agnostically 使用，大幅增强诊断工具的通用性。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_021: Cheetah Run trained dt_emb (collapse replication)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: >\n      跨环境复现 delusional critic collapse：trained dt_embedding \n      在 Cheetah Run 中触发同样的 v/e overshoot → collapse 机制。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_peak: 420\n      seed0_eval_peak_step: 35K\n      seed0_eval_55K: 280\n      seed1_eval_peak: 390\n      seed2_eval_peak: 440\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_35K_mean: 1.85\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_45K_mean: 2.20\n      peak_normalized_ve_max: 2.40\n      collapse_count: \"3/3\"\n      vs_baseline_best_pct: 52\n    result_rationale: >\n      trained dt_embedding → delusional critic 的机制与环境无关，\n      只取决于 RSSM 在 dt=2 transition 上的 fidelity gap。\n      Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 比 Walker Walk 复杂（更高维的速度控制），\n      RSSM 的 dt=2 prediction error 可能更大 → collapse 可能更快更剧烈。\n      peak normalized v/e 在 1.5-2.5x（best tier 定义），\n      因为 dt_embedding 让 critic 学到了 Cheetah Run 中 dt=2 specific \n      的 value pattern，但 RSSM 对这些 pattern 的预测同样不准确。\n      collapse 的时间可能略有提前（Cheetah Run 的更大 prediction error \n      → 更快的 positive feedback），peak return 约为 baseline 的 50-55%\n      （vs Walker 中 008d 的 ~18%，因为 collapse 发生得更快，\n      在 agent 还没充分学习时就开始）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Environment Collapse Comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Environment\", \"Config\", \"Peak Return (% baseline)\", \"Norm v/e at collapse\", \"Seeds collapsed\"]\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"008d\", \"167 (18%)\", \"2.09x@45K\", \"3/3\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run (pred)\", \"trained dt_emb\", \"~420 (52%)\", \"~2.20x@45K\", \"3/3\"]\n          - [\"Mechanism\", \"\", \"Same: trained dt_emb → v/e divergence → collapse\", \"\", \"\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"双环境 collapse 对比图：上排 Walker Walk，下排 Cheetah Run。每排显示 eval return（左）和 normalized v/e（右）。两排均显示相同的 inverted-V + accelerating v/e pattern，标题 'Same mechanism, different environment'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah Run 的 collapse 复现是论文 generalization claim 的支柱。\n      同一机制（trained dt_emb → v/e >1.5x → collapse）在两个\n      dynamics 完全不同的环境中出现，排除了 \"这只是 Walker Walk 的 artifact\" \n      的质疑。normalized v/e 的 pathological threshold（1.5x）在两环境中\n      都成立，确认了它作为 environment-agnostic 诊断工具的价值。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_022: Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 (causal control)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: >\n      跨环境复现 causal control：移除 dt_embedding 消除 Cheetah Run \n      中的 delusional critic，normalized v/e <1.0x。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_55K: 210\n      seed1_eval_55K: 195\n      seed2_eval_55K: 225\n      three_seed_eval_55K_mean: 210\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_35K_mean: 0.75\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_55K_mean: 0.82\n      collapse: false\n      vs_baseline_55K_pct: 26\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Walker Walk 的 008f 完全平行的逻辑：dt_embed_dim=0 移除了\n      critic 的 dt conditioning 通路，阻止了 dt-specific overestimation。\n      Cheetah Run 中绝对性能更低（~210 vs Walker 的 ~230），\n      因为 Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更复杂，subsample ON + H=8 的\n      learning signal 更加不足。但关键指标 normalized v/e <1.0x \n      与 Walker Walk 一致，证明 protection 来自架构（无 dt_emb），\n      不来自环境特性。best tier 定义 cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve \n      在 [0.5, 0.95]，预测 0.82 在此范围内。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah Run: dt_emb=0 vs trained dt_emb\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Metric\", \"dt_embed_dim=0 (pred)\", \"trained dt_emb (pred)\"]\n          - [\"Eval @55K mean\", \"~210\", \"~280 (declining)\"]\n          - [\"Norm v/e @35K mean\", \"0.75x\", \"1.85x\"]\n          - [\"Norm v/e @55K mean\", \"0.82x\", \"collapse\"]\n          - [\"Collapse?\", \"0/3\", \"3/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah Run 版本的 008f vs 008d box plot，格式与 Walker Walk 图一致，展示 cross-environment consistency。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah Run 的 causal control 完成了双环境 × 多种子的验证矩阵：\n      Walker: 008f stable 3/3, 008d collapse 3/3。\n      Cheetah: no-dt-emb stable 3/3, trained-dt-emb collapse 3/3。\n      4 个 condition × 3 seeds = 12 个数据点，全部与因果假设一致。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_023: Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb (value suppression)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: >\n      跨环境复现 C3：untrained dt_emb 在 Cheetah Run 中同样实现\n      value growth suppression 和 near-baseline recovery。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 620\n      seed1_eval_105K: 580\n      seed2_eval_105K: 660\n      three_seed_mean_105K: 620\n      three_seed_vs_baseline_pct: 77\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_105K_mean: 0.62\n      v_recovery_observed: \"2/3 seeds show V-recovery pattern\"\n      collapse: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      untrained dt_emb 在 Cheetah Run 中的 protection 机制相同：\n      random fixed embedding 阻断 dt-conditioned value learning。\n      subsample OFF + H=15 提供足够的 learning signal，\n      因此 agent 能恢复到 baseline 的 70-90%（best tier 定义 [70, 90]，\n      预测 77%）。V-recovery pattern 可能在 2/3 seeds 中可见\n      （Cheetah Run 的更大探索空间可能导致部分 seed 的振荡更不规则），\n      但所有 3 seeds 都不 collapse。normalized v/e 一致 <1.0x。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Environment C3 Comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Environment\", \"Config\", \"Eval@105K (%baseline)\", \"Norm v/e@105K\", \"V-recovery\"]\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"008a (3 seeds)\", \"769±46 (84%)\", \"0.59±0.04x\", \"3/3\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run (pred)\", \"untrained dt_emb\", \"620±40 (77%)\", \"0.62±0.05x\", \"2-3/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"双环境 V-recovery 对比：Walker Walk（上）和 Cheetah Run（下）的 008a-equivalent 学习曲线，均显示振荡但不 collapse 的 pattern。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah Run 中 77% baseline 略低于 Walker Walk 的 84%，\n      符合预期（Cheetah Run dynamics 更复杂 → 更大的 dt=2 prediction error \n      → 即使没有 dt_emb exploitation，RSSM fidelity gap 仍然限制了\n      absolute performance）。但 \"不 collapse\" 和 \"v/e <1.0x\" 的定性结论\n      跨环境一致，支持 C3 的 generalizability。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_030: RSSM prediction quality analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: >\n      直接量化 RSSM 在 dt=1 vs dt=2 transition 上的 fidelity gap，\n      为因果链提供 mechanistic foundation。\n    expected_results:\n      dt1_obs_reconstruction_loss: 0.42\n      dt2_obs_reconstruction_loss: 1.15\n      dt1_reward_prediction_loss: 0.08\n      dt2_reward_prediction_loss: 0.31\n      fidelity_ratio_obs: 2.74\n      fidelity_ratio_reward: 3.88\n    result_rationale: >\n      RSSM 是为 dt=1 sequential prediction 设计的（z_t → z_{t+1}），\n      dt=2 要求跳过一个中间状态直接预测 z_{t+2}。\n      即使通过 subsample ON 训练了 dt=2 transition，RSSM 的 recurrent \n      structure（GRU-based）在跳过时间步时天然会损失信息——\n      中间状态的 dynamics 被 \"折叠\" 进一次 transition，增加了预测不确定性。\n      observation reconstruction loss 的 fidelity ratio ~2.7x \n      反映了这种信息损失；reward prediction 的 ratio 更高（~3.9x）\n      因为 reward 对 state 的微小偏差更敏感（Walker Walk 的 reward \n      是 smooth function of joint angles，dt=2 的 angle prediction error \n      直接放大到 reward error）。\n      这个 fidelity gap 是整个因果链的物理基础：\n      如果 RSSM 能完美预测 dt=2，trained dt_embedding 就不会导致 \n      delusional critic，因为 value estimate 会基于准确的 world model。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RSSM Fidelity Gap\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Metric\", \"dt=1\", \"dt=2\", \"Ratio (dt=2/dt=1)\"]\n          - [\"Obs reconstruction loss\", \"0.42\", \"1.15\", \"2.74x\"]\n          - [\"Reward prediction loss\", \"0.08\", \"0.31\", \"3.88x\"]\n          - [\"State prediction MSE\", \"0.015\", \"0.048\", \"3.20x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart：dt=1 vs dt=2 的三类 loss（obs, reward, state），每组两个 bar。dt=2 bar 上方标注 ratio。标题 'RSSM Fidelity Gap: The Mechanistic Foundation'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      这个分析将因果链从 \"statistical correlation\"（v/e overshoot → collapse）\n      延伸到 \"mechanistic explanation\"（RSSM prediction error at dt=2 \n      → critic exploitation → overestimation）。fidelity ratio 的大小\n      也解释了为什么 dt=4 比 dt=2 更糟糕（C4）：prediction error \n      随 dt 非线性增长。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_031: Actor entropy analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: >\n      分析 collapsed vs healthy config 的 actor entropy 轨迹，\n      检验 \"delusional critic → actor confusion\" 的因果路径。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_entropy_trend: \"monotonic decrease 2.5→1.2 over 100K\"\n      exp_008a_entropy_trend: \"oscillating 2.3→1.8 with V-recovery dips\"\n      exp_008d_entropy_25K: 2.1\n      exp_008d_entropy_35K: 2.4\n      exp_008d_entropy_45K: 2.6\n      exp_008d_entropy_trend: \"increasing from 25K (collapse onset)\"\n      exp_006_entropy_45K: 2.3\n      exp_006_entropy_55K: 2.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      健康的训练过程中，actor entropy 应单调下降：policy 从均匀分布\n      逐渐收敛到高 reward 的 deterministic action。\n      在 delusional critic 场景下，critic 提供的梯度方向不一致\n      （因为 value overestimate 的方向随 imagination trajectory 变化），\n      导致 actor 无法收敛 → entropy 停止下降甚至反弹上升。\n      008d 在 25K（collapse onset）后 entropy 从 2.1 上升到 2.6，\n      表明 actor 在 delusional gradients 下变得越来越 \"confused\"。\n      008a（untrained dt_emb）的 entropy 振荡对应 V-recovery pattern：\n      actor 偶尔找到好 policy（entropy 下降）但 noisy gradient \n      让它偏离（entropy 回升），整体呈缓慢下降趋势而非上升。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Actor Entropy Trajectories\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Step\", \"Baseline\", \"008a (untrained)\", \"008d (trained)\", \"006 (trained)\"]\n          - [\"25K\", \"2.2\", \"2.4\", \"2.1 (collapse start)\", \"2.0\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"2.0\", \"2.3\", \"2.4 ↑\", \"2.1\"]\n          - [\"45K\", \"1.8\", \"2.1\", \"2.6 ↑↑\", \"2.3 ↑\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"1.6\", \"2.0\", \"—\", \"2.7 ↑↑\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"四条 entropy 曲线：baseline（黑，单调下降），008a（蓝，振荡下降），008d（红，collapse 后上升），006（橙，同 008d 模式但延迟）。collapse 区间用红色 shading 标注。\"\n    analysis: >\n      actor entropy 上升是 delusional critic → policy degradation \n      因果路径的直接证据。这补充了 v/e ratio 的诊断（v/e 描述 \"critic 有问题\"，\n      entropy 描述 \"actor 因此受害\"），使因果链的 \"最后一环\" 可观测。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_032: Value prediction distribution\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: >\n      对比 trained vs untrained dt_emb 的 V(s) 分布 vs Monte Carlo return \n      分布，展示 overestimation 的 distributional 特征。\n    expected_results:\n      trained_dtEmb_V_mean_vs_MC_mean_ratio: 1.65\n      trained_dtEmb_V_right_tail_95th: \"3.2x MC 95th\"\n      untrained_dtEmb_V_mean_vs_MC_mean_ratio: 0.92\n      untrained_dtEmb_V_right_tail_95th: \"1.1x MC 95th\"\n      baseline_V_mean_vs_MC_mean_ratio: 1.05\n    result_rationale: >\n      trained dt_emb 导致 critic 系统性高估某些 state-dt combinations，\n      但不是均匀高估——overestimation 集中在 dt=2 imagination trajectory \n      经过的 state 区域。因此 V(s) 分布相比 MC return 分布呈现\n      右偏（right-skewed）：大部分 state 的 V 估计合理，\n      但一小部分 state 的 V 被严重高估（right tail 膨胀 3.2x），\n      而这些 state 恰好是 actor 会在 imagination 中频繁访问的区域\n      → 形成正反馈。untrained dt_emb 的 V 分布几乎匹配 MC 分布\n      （ratio 0.92，略 underestimate——conservative is safe），\n      right tail 无异常膨胀。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三行 histogram overlay（V(s) 蓝色 vs MC return 橙色）：第一行 baseline（几乎重叠），第二行 untrained dt_emb（V 略左偏），第三行 trained dt_emb（V 分布明显右偏，right tail 远超 MC）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Distributional analysis 直接回应 reviewer R3（\"v/e ratio is crude\"），\n      展示 overestimation 不是均匀的而是 state-dependent 的右偏，\n      这比单一 ratio 更 informative，且与 MBRL 文献中的 model exploitation \n      理论一致（agent 学会 exploit model error 最大的 state 区域）。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_033: dt_embedding cosine similarity\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: >\n      追踪 trained dt_embedding 中 dt=1 vs dt=2 向量的 cosine similarity \n      随训练的变化，观察 differentiation 与 collapse 的时间关系。\n    expected_results:\n      cosine_sim_init: 0.85\n      cosine_sim_15K: 0.62\n      cosine_sim_25K: 0.41\n      cosine_sim_35K: 0.28\n      cosine_sim_collapse_onset: \"~0.4 (25K, matching collapse onset)\"\n      untrained_cosine_sim: \"~0.85 (constant, random init)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      初始化时 dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding 是随机向量，cosine similarity ~0.85\n      （高维空间中随机向量的 typical similarity）。\n      训练过程中，RSSM 通过 dt_embedding 学习区分 dt=1 和 dt=2 transition，\n      两个向量逐渐分离（cosine sim 下降）。当 similarity 降到 ~0.4 时，\n      critic 已经能显著区分 dt=1 和 dt=2 的 value estimate，\n      此时如果 dt=2 的 value estimate 基于不准确的 RSSM prediction，\n      delusional overestimation 开始主导。这个时间点（~25K）与 008d 的\n      collapse onset 一致，提供了 dt_embedding differentiation → collapse \n      的 temporal coupling 证据。untrained embedding 的 cosine sim \n      恒定在 ~0.85，永远不会 trigger 这个 differentiation→exploitation 路径。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"dt_embedding Differentiation Timeline\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Step\", \"Cosine Sim\", \"Norm v/e (008d)\", \"Event\"]\n          - [\"5K\", \"0.85\", \"—\", \"embeddings undifferentiated\"]\n          - [\"15K\", \"0.62\", \"—\", \"beginning to separate\"]\n          - [\"25K\", \"0.41\", \"1.78x\", \"collapse onset — critic differentiates dt\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"0.28\", \"1.71x\", \"full differentiation, collapse accelerating\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"双 Y 轴图：左轴 cosine similarity（蓝，下降），右轴 008d normalized v/e（红，上升）。两条曲线交叉区域标注 'critical window: differentiation enables exploitation'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      cosine similarity 分析建立了 dt_embedding training dynamics \n      与 delusional critic onset 的 temporal coupling。\n      这不是相关性而是因果路径上的中间变量：\n      training → embedding differentiation → dt-conditioned value learning \n      → exploitation of RSSM error → collapse。\n      untrained embedding 的恒定 similarity 解释了为什么 protection 是 structural。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_040: Hopper Hop validation (P2, stretch)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: >\n      第三个 DMC 环境验证，强化 generalization claim。\n      3 configs = baseline + trained dt_emb + dt_embed_dim=0。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_asymptotic_mean: 250\n      baseline_asymptotic_std: 30\n      trained_dtEmb_collapse: \"3/3 seeds\"\n      trained_dtEmb_peak_normalized_ve: 1.70\n      no_dtEmb_normalized_ve_55K: 0.80\n      no_dtEmb_eval_55K_vs_baseline_pct: 28\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 是 DMC 中难度较高的环境（DreamerV3 baseline ~200-300），\n      RSSM 对 hopping dynamics 的建模难度更大（contact dynamics, \n      discontinuous state transitions）。因此 dt=2 的 RSSM fidelity gap \n      可能更大 → trained dt_emb 的 collapse 可能更快。\n      但在 best tier 下，同一机制仍然 hold：\n      trained dt_emb → v/e >1.5x → collapse；no dt_emb → v/e <1.0x → stable。\n      有了三个环境的一致结果，论文可以 claim \"the mechanism generalizes \n      across DMC locomotion tasks\"。Hopper Hop 是 P2 stretch goal，\n      不是 blocking，但如果完成，将使 generalization claim 从 \n      \"two environments\" 升级为 \"three diverse environments\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Three-Environment Mechanism Consistency\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Environment\", \"Trained dt_emb collapse\", \"No dt_emb stable\", \"Norm v/e threshold holds\"]\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"3/3 ✓\", \"3/3 ✓\", \"✓ (1.5x)\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run (pred)\", \"3/3 ✓\", \"3/3 ✓\", \"✓ (1.5x)\"]\n          - [\"Hopper Hop (pred)\", \"3/3 ✓\", \"3/3 ✓\", \"✓ (1.5x)\"]\n          - [\"Total\", \"9/9\", \"9/9\", \"100% consistent\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3×2 panel：三行（三个环境），两列（eval return, normalized v/e）。每个 panel 叠加 trained dt_emb（红）和 no dt_emb（蓝）。所有红线 collapse，所有蓝线 stable，视觉上极具冲击力。\"\n    analysis: >\n      三环境 × 多种子 = 论文最强的泛化证据。\n      9/9 collapse + 9/9 stable 的 binary 一致性使得 p-value < 0.001\n      （binomial test），即使不做 formal hypothesis testing，\n      reviewer 也很难质疑机制的 generality。\n      但 Hopper Hop 是 45 GPU-hours，在 deadline 前可能无法完成。\n      即使没有 Hopper Hop，Walker + Cheetah 的 6/6 + 6/6 已经足够。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20446,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20446},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bef9a362-8ebf-4bcb-9f30-9fef8cba03ac","uuid":"b2e30d44-f560-420b-8d08-ad6268cc87ba"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":297093,"duration_api_ms":299057,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  完整因果诊断论文。标题 \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails\"。\n  核心因果链：trained dt_embedding → RSSM fidelity gap → delusional critic → collapse，\n  经 factorial ablation + 双环境 + 多种子三重验证闭合。\n  v/e overshoot ratio >1.5x 作为可复用诊断工具。C2 升级为 confirmed。\n  Discussion 明确建议：不要在当前 RSSM 架构中联合训练 dt_embedding。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: 008f 继续运行至 55K（已有 35K 数据）\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk dt_embed_dim=0 H=8 — 55K completion\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      008f 已运行至 35K，继续至 55K+ 确认 normalized v/e 持续收敛，\n      eval 稳定在 190-260 范围，与 008d 的 diverging pattern 形成完整对照。\n    expected_results:\n      eval_return_45K: 215\n      eval_return_55K: 230\n      eval_return_65K: 238\n      value_mean_45K: 55.0\n      value_mean_55K: 76.0\n      value_eval_ratio_45K: 0.256\n      value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.330\n      normalized_ve_45K: 0.77\n      normalized_ve_55K: 0.82\n      normalized_ve_65K: 0.72\n      vs_baseline_55K: \"-63.2%\"\n      collapse: false\n      gate_dt_mean: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      dt_embed_dim=0 意味着 critic 在 imagination 中无法获得 dt 信息，\n      因此无法对 dt=2 步骤做出 dt-specific 的价值估计。\n      RSSM 仍然用 dt=2 transition 训练（subsample ON），所以 world model \n      对 dt=2 dynamics 的预测质量仍然有限，限制了绝对性能（~230 vs baseline 950）。\n      但关键是：没有 dt_embedding → critic 不会因 dt-conditioned \n      overestimation 而 diverge。v/e 应跟随或略低于 baseline 的自然增长曲线\n      （normalized ~0.7-0.85x），绝不会出现 008d 那种 >1.5x 的 pathological \n      overshoot。45K→55K 的 normalized v/e 从 0.77→0.82 是自然漂移，\n      不是 accelerating divergence。这直接证明 dt_embedding conditioning \n      （而非 RSSM 的 dt=2 dynamics 本身）是 delusional critic 的 root cause。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008f vs 008d — Causal Isolation\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Metric\", \"008f (no dt_emb)\", \"008d (trained dt_emb)\", \"Interpretation\"]\n          - [\"normalized_ve_25K\", \"1.02x\", \"1.78x\", \"008d 已进入 pathological\"]\n          - [\"normalized_ve_35K\", \"0.73x\", \"1.71x\", \"008f 收敛，008d 持续 diverge\"]\n          - [\"normalized_ve_45K\", \"0.77x (pred)\", \"2.09x\", \"gap 扩大至 2.7x 差异\"]\n          - [\"normalized_ve_55K\", \"0.82x (pred)\", \"— (已 collapse)\", \"008f 稳定\"]\n          - [\"eval_return_45K\", \"~215 (pred)\", \"140.8\", \"008f 略高，无 collapse\"]\n          - [\"collapse\", \"No\", \"Yes (@35K)\", \"单变量隔离确认\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"双 Y 轴图：左轴 normalized v/e ratio，右轴 eval return。008f（蓝，实线）和 008d（红，虚线）并排。008d 的 v/e 从 1.78x→2.09x 加速上升同时 eval 下降形成 'X 交叉'；008f 的 v/e 在 0.7-0.85x 水平波动，eval 缓慢上升。灰色水平线标注 1.5x pathological threshold。\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是整篇论文的 smoking gun。008f 与 008d 仅差一个变量：dt_embedding。\n      008d 有 trained dt_embedding → normalized v/e 1.78x→2.09x → collapse；\n      008f 无 dt_embedding → normalized v/e 0.73x→0.82x → stable。\n      因果归因闭合：dt_embedding conditioning 是 delusional critic 的充要条件。\n      RSSM 的 dt=2 prediction quality 本身不足以触发 collapse（008f 证明），\n      但给 critic 提供 dt 信息后，critic 会 exploit 这些不准确的 dt-conditioned \n      predictions 来系统性高估 value。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: 008e_v2 — untrained dt_emb + subsample ON + H=15\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk untrained dt_emb + subsample ON H=15\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      解耦 008a 的 B+ protection 来源：是 untrained dt_emb 还是 subsample OFF？\n      008e_v3 已在运行（45K 数据：382.2, v/e=0.876x），预测完整轨迹。\n    expected_results:\n      eval_return_45K: 382\n      eval_return_55K: 430\n      eval_return_65K: 490\n      eval_return_75K: 460\n      eval_return_85K: 520\n      eval_return_95K: 550\n      eval_return_105K: 640\n      value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.36\n      value_eval_ratio_65K: 0.40\n      value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.45\n      normalized_ve_45K: 0.88\n      normalized_ve_55K: 0.89\n      normalized_ve_65K: 0.71\n      normalized_ve_105K: 0.69\n      vs_baseline_105K: \"-30.1%\"\n      collapse: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      untrained dt_emb + subsample ON + H=15 结合了两个效应：\n      (1) untrained dt_emb 阻止 dt-conditioned value overestimation（同 008a 机制），\n      (2) subsample ON 减少有效训练 transition 数量，比 008a（subsample OFF）学得慢。\n      因此绝对性能低于 008a（640 vs 778 @105K），但同样不会 collapse。\n      normalized v/e 保持 <1.0x 证明 protection 来自 untrained dt_emb（而非 subsample OFF），\n      因为 subsample ON 的训练数据分布与 008d 相同，唯一差异是 dt_emb 是否 trained。\n      相比 008a 的两次 V-recovery，这里预期振荡幅度更小（subsample ON \n      → 更稳定但更慢的学习信号），呈现缓慢单调上升而非剧烈 V 形。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"B+ Protection 归因：008a vs 008e_v2 vs 008d\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Config\", \"subsample\", \"dt_emb\", \"eval@105K\", \"norm_ve@105K\", \"collapse\"]\n          - [\"008a\", \"OFF\", \"untrained\", \"778\", \"0.59x\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"008e_v2 (pred)\", \"ON\", \"untrained\", \"~640\", \"~0.69x\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"008d\", \"ON\", \"trained\", \"— (collapse@35K)\", \"2.09x@45K\", \"Yes\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三条学习曲线叠加：008a（蓝）显示 V-recovery 到 778，008e_v2（绿）显示较慢但稳定的上升到 ~640，008d（红）显示 35K 后 collapse。下方子图显示 normalized v/e，008a 和 008e_v2 均在 1.0x 以下，008d 在 1.5x 以上。\"\n    analysis: >\n      008e_v2 是 C3/C5 的关键解耦实验。如果 008a 的 protection 来自 subsample OFF\n      （更多训练数据），那么 008e_v2（subsample ON）应该 collapse。\n      但 008e_v2 不 collapse 且 normalized v/e <1.0x，证明 protection \n      的主因是 untrained dt_emb，subsample 只影响收敛速度。\n      这也强化了 C5：learning signal reduction 是 secondary factor，不是 root cause。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_010: Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      2 个额外 seed 建立 baseline v/e 校准的置信区间，\n      为 008d/008f 多种子 normalized v/e 计算提供 per-seed reference。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_last10_mean: 940\n      seed2_eval_return_last10_mean: 960\n      three_seed_mean: 950.3\n      three_seed_std: 9.5\n      seed1_ve_35K: 0.23\n      seed2_ve_35K: 0.25\n      seed1_ve_55K: 0.39\n      seed2_ve_55K: 0.42\n      seed1_ve_105K: 0.64\n      seed2_ve_105K: 0.68\n      ve_35K_mean: 0.240\n      ve_35K_std: 0.013\n      ve_55K_mean: 0.405\n      ve_55K_std: 0.015\n      ve_105K_mean: 0.660\n      ve_105K_std: 0.014\n      ve_stable_range: \"68-73%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker Walk 是 DMC 中最稳定的环境之一，DreamerV3 baseline 的 seed 间方差极小。\n      seed 0 的 asymptotic 950.9 ± ~10 是典型值。v/e ratio 的 seed 间方差\n      主要来自 eval return 的随机波动（±15-20），而 value function 的收敛轨迹\n      高度一致（因为 world model 在此简单环境中很快收敛）。\n      三种子均值 ~950、std <10 为后续所有 normalized v/e 计算提供了\n      robust 的 per-step reference curve，使得 \"1.5x = pathological\" \n      的 threshold 具有统计意义（而非单种子巧合）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Baseline v/e Calibration (3 seeds)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Step\", \"Seed 0\", \"Seed 1 (pred)\", \"Seed 2 (pred)\", \"Mean±Std\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"0.241\", \"0.23\", \"0.25\", \"0.240±0.013\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"0.404\", \"0.39\", \"0.42\", \"0.405±0.015\"]\n          - [\"105K\", \"0.656\", \"0.64\", \"0.68\", \"0.660±0.014\"]\n          - [\"Asymptotic\", \"~70%\", \"~69%\", \"~72%\", \"~70±1.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"v/e ratio vs training step 带 shaded confidence band（3 seeds）。中线为均值，shaded region 为 ±1 std。水平虚线标注 asymptotic ~70%。此图作为后续所有 normalized v/e 计算的 reference。\"\n    analysis: >\n      baseline 多种子的意义不在于确认 Walker Walk 能解决（这是 trivial 的），\n      而在于建立 v/e ratio 的 per-step reference distribution。\n      单种子 normalized v/e 有 ±5-8% 的 noise，三种子均值将 noise 降到 ±3-4%，\n      使得 \"008d 的 1.7x 是 pathological\" 的判断从 \"很可能\" 升级为 \"统计显著\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_011: Walker Walk 008d seeds 1-2 (collapse replication)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      复现 delusional critic collapse：3/3 seeds 均应在 25K-45K \n      出现 normalized v/e >1.5x 并触发 eval return 持续下降。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_25K: 155\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 138\n      seed1_eval_return_45K: 125\n      seed2_eval_return_25K: 172\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 152\n      seed2_eval_return_45K: 133\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.62\n      seed1_normalized_ve_45K: 1.95\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.80\n      seed2_normalized_ve_45K: 2.15\n      three_seed_collapse_count: 3\n      three_seed_peak_return_mean: 165\n      three_seed_peak_return_std: 12\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_45K_mean: 2.06\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_45K_std: 0.13\n    result_rationale: >\n      trained dt_embedding 导致的 delusional critic 是结构性问题，不是随机事件。\n      机制：trained dt_emb 让 critic 在 imagination 中为 dt=2 步骤学到\n      dt-specific 的 value estimate，但 RSSM 在 dt=2 transition 上的\n      prediction fidelity 不足以支撑这种精度 → critic 系统性高估 → actor \n      追逐虚假梯度 → eval return 下降 → 正反馈循环。\n      这个机制对初始化不敏感（dt_embedding 的训练方向由 RSSM 的 dt=2 \n      prediction bias 决定，而该 bias 在不同 seed 中方向一致——都是 overestimate），\n      因此预期 3/3 seeds 全部 collapse，seed 间 normalized v/e 的方差很小（±0.13）。\n      collapse 的时间点可能有 ±5K step 的偏差，但模式完全一致。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008d Collapse Replication (3 seeds)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Metric\", \"Seed 0\", \"Seed 1 (pred)\", \"Seed 2 (pred)\", \"Consistency\"]\n          - [\"Peak eval return\", \"167@25K\", \"155@25K\", \"172@25K\", \"Mean 165±9\"]\n          - [\"Eval @45K\", \"140.8\", \"~125\", \"~133\", \"All declining\"]\n          - [\"Norm v/e @35K\", \"1.71x\", \"1.62x\", \"1.80x\", \"All >1.5x ✓\"]\n          - [\"Norm v/e @45K\", \"2.09x\", \"1.95x\", \"2.15x\", \"All >1.5x ✓\"]\n          - [\"Collapse?\", \"Yes\", \"Yes\", \"Yes\", \"3/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三条 eval return 曲线（红色系，不同 line style 区分 seed）全部呈 inverted-V 后持续下降。右侧子图显示 normalized v/e 全部 >1.5x（灰色 threshold 线以上）。配对标注 '3/3 seeds collapse'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      3/3 collapse 复现是 best tier 的 defining criterion 之一。\n      这将 C2 从 \"provisional\" 升级为 \"confirmed\"，因为 collapse 不是\n      单种子的随机异常，而是 trained dt_embedding 的必然结果。\n      reviewer R6 的 \"single seed\" concern 被直接消解。\n      seed 间一致性（normalized v/e std ~0.13）还表明 1.5x threshold \n      是 robust 的诊断标准，不需要 per-seed calibration。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_012: Walker Walk 008f seeds 1-2 (stability replication)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: >\n      复现 causal control 的稳定性：3/3 seeds 的 normalized v/e \n      持续 <1.0x，无 collapse，与 008d 形成完美对照。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 220\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 240\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 0.70\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.78\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 0.76\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.85\n      three_seed_eval_55K_mean: 232\n      three_seed_eval_55K_std: 16\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_55K_mean: 0.80\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_55K_std: 0.06\n      three_seed_stable_count: 3\n      collapse: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      dt_embed_dim=0 从架构上消除了 dt conditioning 通路。\n      无论 seed 如何变化，critic 都无法获得 dt 信息，因此无法形成\n      dt-specific 的 overestimation。这是架构级的保护，不依赖初始化。\n      性能低（~230 vs baseline 950）是因为 subsample ON 减少了训练数据\n      且 H=8 horizon 太短，但这与 collapse 是完全不同的 failure mode。\n      normalized v/e 在 0.7-0.85x 范围的 seed 间方差来自 eval return \n      的随机波动，不会突破 1.0x，更不会到 1.5x pathological zone。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008f vs 008d 多种子对照\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"\", \"008f norm_ve (3 seeds)\", \"008d norm_ve (3 seeds)\"]\n          - [\"@35K\", \"0.73, 0.70, 0.76\", \"1.71, 1.62, 1.80\"]\n          - [\"@55K\", \"0.82, 0.78, 0.85\", \"collapse, collapse, collapse\"]\n          - [\"Mean±Std @35K\", \"0.73±0.03\", \"1.71±0.09\"]\n          - [\"Collapse rate\", \"0/3\", \"3/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot 或 violin plot：x 轴为 config（008f vs 008d），y 轴为 normalized v/e @35K。008f 的分布完全在 1.0x 以下，008d 完全在 1.5x 以上，无重叠。1.5x threshold 水平线标注。\"\n    analysis: >\n      008f 3/3 stable + 008d 3/3 collapse = 完美的 6-point causal contrast。\n      effect size 极大（Cohen's d > 10），统计检验的 p-value 可以忽略。\n      这直接回答了论文的核心问题：为什么 temporal abstraction 失败？\n      答案：因为 trained dt_embedding 让 critic exploit RSSM 的 fidelity gap。\n      移除 dt_embedding → 移除 exploit 通路 → 消除 collapse。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_013: Walker Walk 008a seeds 1-2 (V-recovery replication)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: >\n      复现 value growth suppression 和 V-recovery pattern，\n      确认 untrained dt_emb 的保护效应跨 seed 一致。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_65K: 580\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 720\n      seed2_eval_return_65K: 630\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 810\n      three_seed_mean_105K: 769\n      three_seed_std_105K: 46\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.62\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.55\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_105K_mean: 0.59\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_105K_std: 0.04\n      v_recovery_count: \"3/3 show at least one V-recovery\"\n      collapse: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      untrained dt_emb 的 protection 机制是架构性的（random fixed embedding \n      阻断 dt-specific value learning），因此 V-recovery pattern 应跨 seed 复现。\n      但 V-recovery 的具体时间和幅度受 exploration noise 影响较大：\n      actor 在 random dt_embedding 下的梯度信号较弱且含噪，导致 policy \n      在局部最优间振荡（V 的下降段），然后通过 value function 的 slow \n      catch-up 恢复（V 的上升段）。seed 0 有两次 V-recovery，\n      其他 seed 可能只有一次或三次，但模式一致：振荡但不 collapse。\n      三种子均值 769±46 @105K 对应 baseline 的 84%（best tier 定义 700-850），\n      normalized v/e 均值 0.59±0.04 远低于 pathological threshold。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008a V-Recovery Replication (3 seeds)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Seed\", \"Peak@65K\", \"Dip (min after peak)\", \"@105K\", \"Norm v/e@105K\", \"V-recoveries\"]\n          - [\"Seed 0\", \"608\", \"470@75K\", \"778\", \"0.59x\", \"2\"]\n          - [\"Seed 1 (pred)\", \"580\", \"440@75K\", \"720\", \"0.62x\", \"1-2\"]\n          - [\"Seed 2 (pred)\", \"630\", \"490@85K\", \"810\", \"0.55x\", \"2\"]\n          - [\"Mean±Std\", \"606±25\", \"467±25\", \"769±46\", \"0.59±0.04\", \"All ≥1\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三条 eval return 曲线（蓝色系）叠加显示 V-recovery pattern，每条都有振荡但无 collapse。shaded band 显示 ±1 std。下方子图 normalized v/e 三条线全部在 1.0x 以下且随训练递减。\"\n    analysis: >\n      V-recovery 的多种子复现证明这是 untrained dt_emb 的系统性行为，\n      而非 seed 0 的巧合。振荡的存在表明 dt=2 imagination 仍然引入了\n      learning instability（vs baseline 的 smooth convergence），\n      但 untrained dt_emb 将 instability 的上界限制在 \"振荡\" 而非 \"collapse\"。\n      这支持 C3 的核心论点：untrained dt_emb substantively protects performance。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_020: Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: >\n      建立 Cheetah Run 的 dt=1 reference，包括 asymptotic return \n      和 v/e calibration curve，为跨环境泛化提供 second environment anchor。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_asymptotic: 810\n      seed1_eval_return_asymptotic: 790\n      seed2_eval_return_asymptotic: 830\n      three_seed_mean_asymptotic: 810\n      three_seed_std_asymptotic: 20\n      ve_35K_mean: 0.21\n      ve_55K_mean: 0.38\n      ve_105K_mean: 0.60\n      ve_stable_range: \"62-68%\"\n      fps: 7.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah Run 在 DreamerV3 中的典型 asymptotic return 为 780-850。\n      相比 Walker Walk（~950），Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更复杂\n      （连续前进、速度控制），但 RSSM 仍能有效建模 dt=1 transition。\n      v/e ratio 的增长曲线与 Walker Walk 类似但 asymptotic 略低（~65% vs ~70%），\n      因为 Cheetah Run 的 reward scale 和 episode structure 不同，\n      value function 的 calibration 稍有差异。\n      三种子方差 std ~20 略高于 Walker Walk（std ~10），因为 Cheetah Run \n      的探索空间更大，不同 seed 可能发现略不同的 gait pattern。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah Run Baseline v/e Calibration\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Step\", \"Mean v/e\", \"Std\", \"vs Walker baseline\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"0.21\", \"0.02\", \"Walker: 0.24 (similar)\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"0.38\", \"0.03\", \"Walker: 0.40 (similar)\"]\n          - [\"105K\", \"0.60\", \"0.03\", \"Walker: 0.66 (slightly lower)\"]\n          - [\"Asymptotic\", \"~65%\", \"~3%\", \"Walker: ~70%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Walker Walk vs Cheetah Run baseline v/e ratio 并排图，显示两个环境的 calibration curve 形状相似但量级略有差异，建立 cross-environment reference。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah Run baseline 的主要目的是为 normalized v/e 计算提供 \n      environment-specific reference。如果两环境的 v/e calibration curve \n      形状一致（都是 monotonic 增长到 asymptotic），则 1.5x threshold \n      可以 environment-agnostically 使用，大幅增强诊断工具的通用性。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_021: Cheetah Run trained dt_emb (collapse replication)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: >\n      跨环境复现 delusional critic collapse：trained dt_embedding \n      在 Cheetah Run 中触发同样的 v/e overshoot → collapse 机制。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_peak: 420\n      seed0_eval_peak_step: 35K\n      seed0_eval_55K: 280\n      seed1_eval_peak: 390\n      seed2_eval_peak: 440\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_35K_mean: 1.85\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_45K_mean: 2.20\n      peak_normalized_ve_max: 2.40\n      collapse_count: \"3/3\"\n      vs_baseline_best_pct: 52\n    result_rationale: >\n      trained dt_embedding → delusional critic 的机制与环境无关，\n      只取决于 RSSM 在 dt=2 transition 上的 fidelity gap。\n      Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 比 Walker Walk 复杂（更高维的速度控制），\n      RSSM 的 dt=2 prediction error 可能更大 → collapse 可能更快更剧烈。\n      peak normalized v/e 在 1.5-2.5x（best tier 定义），\n      因为 dt_embedding 让 critic 学到了 Cheetah Run 中 dt=2 specific \n      的 value pattern，但 RSSM 对这些 pattern 的预测同样不准确。\n      collapse 的时间可能略有提前（Cheetah Run 的更大 prediction error \n      → 更快的 positive feedback），peak return 约为 baseline 的 50-55%\n      （vs Walker 中 008d 的 ~18%，因为 collapse 发生得更快，\n      在 agent 还没充分学习时就开始）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Environment Collapse Comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Environment\", \"Config\", \"Peak Return (% baseline)\", \"Norm v/e at collapse\", \"Seeds collapsed\"]\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"008d\", \"167 (18%)\", \"2.09x@45K\", \"3/3\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run (pred)\", \"trained dt_emb\", \"~420 (52%)\", \"~2.20x@45K\", \"3/3\"]\n          - [\"Mechanism\", \"\", \"Same: trained dt_emb → v/e divergence → collapse\", \"\", \"\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"双环境 collapse 对比图：上排 Walker Walk，下排 Cheetah Run。每排显示 eval return（左）和 normalized v/e（右）。两排均显示相同的 inverted-V + accelerating v/e pattern，标题 'Same mechanism, different environment'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah Run 的 collapse 复现是论文 generalization claim 的支柱。\n      同一机制（trained dt_emb → v/e >1.5x → collapse）在两个\n      dynamics 完全不同的环境中出现，排除了 \"这只是 Walker Walk 的 artifact\" \n      的质疑。normalized v/e 的 pathological threshold（1.5x）在两环境中\n      都成立，确认了它作为 environment-agnostic 诊断工具的价值。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_022: Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 (causal control)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: >\n      跨环境复现 causal control：移除 dt_embedding 消除 Cheetah Run \n      中的 delusional critic，normalized v/e <1.0x。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_55K: 210\n      seed1_eval_55K: 195\n      seed2_eval_55K: 225\n      three_seed_eval_55K_mean: 210\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_35K_mean: 0.75\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_55K_mean: 0.82\n      collapse: false\n      vs_baseline_55K_pct: 26\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Walker Walk 的 008f 完全平行的逻辑：dt_embed_dim=0 移除了\n      critic 的 dt conditioning 通路，阻止了 dt-specific overestimation。\n      Cheetah Run 中绝对性能更低（~210 vs Walker 的 ~230），\n      因为 Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更复杂，subsample ON + H=8 的\n      learning signal 更加不足。但关键指标 normalized v/e <1.0x \n      与 Walker Walk 一致，证明 protection 来自架构（无 dt_emb），\n      不来自环境特性。best tier 定义 cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve \n      在 [0.5, 0.95]，预测 0.82 在此范围内。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah Run: dt_emb=0 vs trained dt_emb\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Metric\", \"dt_embed_dim=0 (pred)\", \"trained dt_emb (pred)\"]\n          - [\"Eval @55K mean\", \"~210\", \"~280 (declining)\"]\n          - [\"Norm v/e @35K mean\", \"0.75x\", \"1.85x\"]\n          - [\"Norm v/e @55K mean\", \"0.82x\", \"collapse\"]\n          - [\"Collapse?\", \"0/3\", \"3/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah Run 版本的 008f vs 008d box plot，格式与 Walker Walk 图一致，展示 cross-environment consistency。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah Run 的 causal control 完成了双环境 × 多种子的验证矩阵：\n      Walker: 008f stable 3/3, 008d collapse 3/3。\n      Cheetah: no-dt-emb stable 3/3, trained-dt-emb collapse 3/3。\n      4 个 condition × 3 seeds = 12 个数据点，全部与因果假设一致。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_023: Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb (value suppression)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: >\n      跨环境复现 C3：untrained dt_emb 在 Cheetah Run 中同样实现\n      value growth suppression 和 near-baseline recovery。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 620\n      seed1_eval_105K: 580\n      seed2_eval_105K: 660\n      three_seed_mean_105K: 620\n      three_seed_vs_baseline_pct: 77\n      three_seed_normalized_ve_105K_mean: 0.62\n      v_recovery_observed: \"2/3 seeds show V-recovery pattern\"\n      collapse: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      untrained dt_emb 在 Cheetah Run 中的 protection 机制相同：\n      random fixed embedding 阻断 dt-conditioned value learning。\n      subsample OFF + H=15 提供足够的 learning signal，\n      因此 agent 能恢复到 baseline 的 70-90%（best tier 定义 [70, 90]，\n      预测 77%）。V-recovery pattern 可能在 2/3 seeds 中可见\n      （Cheetah Run 的更大探索空间可能导致部分 seed 的振荡更不规则），\n      但所有 3 seeds 都不 collapse。normalized v/e 一致 <1.0x。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Environment C3 Comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Environment\", \"Config\", \"Eval@105K (%baseline)\", \"Norm v/e@105K\", \"V-recovery\"]\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"008a (3 seeds)\", \"769±46 (84%)\", \"0.59±0.04x\", \"3/3\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run (pred)\", \"untrained dt_emb\", \"620±40 (77%)\", \"0.62±0.05x\", \"2-3/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"双环境 V-recovery 对比：Walker Walk（上）和 Cheetah Run（下）的 008a-equivalent 学习曲线，均显示振荡但不 collapse 的 pattern。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah Run 中 77% baseline 略低于 Walker Walk 的 84%，\n      符合预期（Cheetah Run dynamics 更复杂 → 更大的 dt=2 prediction error \n      → 即使没有 dt_emb exploitation，RSSM fidelity gap 仍然限制了\n      absolute performance）。但 \"不 collapse\" 和 \"v/e <1.0x\" 的定性结论\n      跨环境一致，支持 C3 的 generalizability。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_030: RSSM prediction quality analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: >\n      直接量化 RSSM 在 dt=1 vs dt=2 transition 上的 fidelity gap，\n      为因果链提供 mechanistic foundation。\n    expected_results:\n      dt1_obs_reconstruction_loss: 0.42\n      dt2_obs_reconstruction_loss: 1.15\n      dt1_reward_prediction_loss: 0.08\n      dt2_reward_prediction_loss: 0.31\n      fidelity_ratio_obs: 2.74\n      fidelity_ratio_reward: 3.88\n    result_rationale: >\n      RSSM 是为 dt=1 sequential prediction 设计的（z_t → z_{t+1}），\n      dt=2 要求跳过一个中间状态直接预测 z_{t+2}。\n      即使通过 subsample ON 训练了 dt=2 transition，RSSM 的 recurrent \n      structure（GRU-based）在跳过时间步时天然会损失信息——\n      中间状态的 dynamics 被 \"折叠\" 进一次 transition，增加了预测不确定性。\n      observation reconstruction loss 的 fidelity ratio ~2.7x \n      反映了这种信息损失；reward prediction 的 ratio 更高（~3.9x）\n      因为 reward 对 state 的微小偏差更敏感（Walker Walk 的 reward \n      是 smooth function of joint angles，dt=2 的 angle prediction error \n      直接放大到 reward error）。\n      这个 fidelity gap 是整个因果链的物理基础：\n      如果 RSSM 能完美预测 dt=2，trained dt_embedding 就不会导致 \n      delusional critic，因为 value estimate 会基于准确的 world model。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RSSM Fidelity Gap\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Metric\", \"dt=1\", \"dt=2\", \"Ratio (dt=2/dt=1)\"]\n          - [\"Obs reconstruction loss\", \"0.42\", \"1.15\", \"2.74x\"]\n          - [\"Reward prediction loss\", \"0.08\", \"0.31\", \"3.88x\"]\n          - [\"State prediction MSE\", \"0.015\", \"0.048\", \"3.20x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart：dt=1 vs dt=2 的三类 loss（obs, reward, state），每组两个 bar。dt=2 bar 上方标注 ratio。标题 'RSSM Fidelity Gap: The Mechanistic Foundation'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      这个分析将因果链从 \"statistical correlation\"（v/e overshoot → collapse）\n      延伸到 \"mechanistic explanation\"（RSSM prediction error at dt=2 \n      → critic exploitation → overestimation）。fidelity ratio 的大小\n      也解释了为什么 dt=4 比 dt=2 更糟糕（C4）：prediction error \n      随 dt 非线性增长。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_031: Actor entropy analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: >\n      分析 collapsed vs healthy config 的 actor entropy 轨迹，\n      检验 \"delusional critic → actor confusion\" 的因果路径。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_entropy_trend: \"monotonic decrease 2.5→1.2 over 100K\"\n      exp_008a_entropy_trend: \"oscillating 2.3→1.8 with V-recovery dips\"\n      exp_008d_entropy_25K: 2.1\n      exp_008d_entropy_35K: 2.4\n      exp_008d_entropy_45K: 2.6\n      exp_008d_entropy_trend: \"increasing from 25K (collapse onset)\"\n      exp_006_entropy_45K: 2.3\n      exp_006_entropy_55K: 2.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      健康的训练过程中，actor entropy 应单调下降：policy 从均匀分布\n      逐渐收敛到高 reward 的 deterministic action。\n      在 delusional critic 场景下，critic 提供的梯度方向不一致\n      （因为 value overestimate 的方向随 imagination trajectory 变化），\n      导致 actor 无法收敛 → entropy 停止下降甚至反弹上升。\n      008d 在 25K（collapse onset）后 entropy 从 2.1 上升到 2.6，\n      表明 actor 在 delusional gradients 下变得越来越 \"confused\"。\n      008a（untrained dt_emb）的 entropy 振荡对应 V-recovery pattern：\n      actor 偶尔找到好 policy（entropy 下降）但 noisy gradient \n      让它偏离（entropy 回升），整体呈缓慢下降趋势而非上升。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Actor Entropy Trajectories\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Step\", \"Baseline\", \"008a (untrained)\", \"008d (trained)\", \"006 (trained)\"]\n          - [\"25K\", \"2.2\", \"2.4\", \"2.1 (collapse start)\", \"2.0\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"2.0\", \"2.3\", \"2.4 ↑\", \"2.1\"]\n          - [\"45K\", \"1.8\", \"2.1\", \"2.6 ↑↑\", \"2.3 ↑\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"1.6\", \"2.0\", \"—\", \"2.7 ↑↑\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"四条 entropy 曲线：baseline（黑，单调下降），008a（蓝，振荡下降），008d（红，collapse 后上升），006（橙，同 008d 模式但延迟）。collapse 区间用红色 shading 标注。\"\n    analysis: >\n      actor entropy 上升是 delusional critic → policy degradation \n      因果路径的直接证据。这补充了 v/e ratio 的诊断（v/e 描述 \"critic 有问题\"，\n      entropy 描述 \"actor 因此受害\"），使因果链的 \"最后一环\" 可观测。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_032: Value prediction distribution\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: >\n      对比 trained vs untrained dt_emb 的 V(s) 分布 vs Monte Carlo return \n      分布，展示 overestimation 的 distributional 特征。\n    expected_results:\n      trained_dtEmb_V_mean_vs_MC_mean_ratio: 1.65\n      trained_dtEmb_V_right_tail_95th: \"3.2x MC 95th\"\n      untrained_dtEmb_V_mean_vs_MC_mean_ratio: 0.92\n      untrained_dtEmb_V_right_tail_95th: \"1.1x MC 95th\"\n      baseline_V_mean_vs_MC_mean_ratio: 1.05\n    result_rationale: >\n      trained dt_emb 导致 critic 系统性高估某些 state-dt combinations，\n      但不是均匀高估——overestimation 集中在 dt=2 imagination trajectory \n      经过的 state 区域。因此 V(s) 分布相比 MC return 分布呈现\n      右偏（right-skewed）：大部分 state 的 V 估计合理，\n      但一小部分 state 的 V 被严重高估（right tail 膨胀 3.2x），\n      而这些 state 恰好是 actor 会在 imagination 中频繁访问的区域\n      → 形成正反馈。untrained dt_emb 的 V 分布几乎匹配 MC 分布\n      （ratio 0.92，略 underestimate——conservative is safe），\n      right tail 无异常膨胀。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三行 histogram overlay（V(s) 蓝色 vs MC return 橙色）：第一行 baseline（几乎重叠），第二行 untrained dt_emb（V 略左偏），第三行 trained dt_emb（V 分布明显右偏，right tail 远超 MC）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Distributional analysis 直接回应 reviewer R3（\"v/e ratio is crude\"），\n      展示 overestimation 不是均匀的而是 state-dependent 的右偏，\n      这比单一 ratio 更 informative，且与 MBRL 文献中的 model exploitation \n      理论一致（agent 学会 exploit model error 最大的 state 区域）。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_033: dt_embedding cosine similarity\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: >\n      追踪 trained dt_embedding 中 dt=1 vs dt=2 向量的 cosine similarity \n      随训练的变化，观察 differentiation 与 collapse 的时间关系。\n    expected_results:\n      cosine_sim_init: 0.85\n      cosine_sim_15K: 0.62\n      cosine_sim_25K: 0.41\n      cosine_sim_35K: 0.28\n      cosine_sim_collapse_onset: \"~0.4 (25K, matching collapse onset)\"\n      untrained_cosine_sim: \"~0.85 (constant, random init)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      初始化时 dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding 是随机向量，cosine similarity ~0.85\n      （高维空间中随机向量的 typical similarity）。\n      训练过程中，RSSM 通过 dt_embedding 学习区分 dt=1 和 dt=2 transition，\n      两个向量逐渐分离（cosine sim 下降）。当 similarity 降到 ~0.4 时，\n      critic 已经能显著区分 dt=1 和 dt=2 的 value estimate，\n      此时如果 dt=2 的 value estimate 基于不准确的 RSSM prediction，\n      delusional overestimation 开始主导。这个时间点（~25K）与 008d 的\n      collapse onset 一致，提供了 dt_embedding differentiation → collapse \n      的 temporal coupling 证据。untrained embedding 的 cosine sim \n      恒定在 ~0.85，永远不会 trigger 这个 differentiation→exploitation 路径。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"dt_embedding Differentiation Timeline\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Step\", \"Cosine Sim\", \"Norm v/e (008d)\", \"Event\"]\n          - [\"5K\", \"0.85\", \"—\", \"embeddings undifferentiated\"]\n          - [\"15K\", \"0.62\", \"—\", \"beginning to separate\"]\n          - [\"25K\", \"0.41\", \"1.78x\", \"collapse onset — critic differentiates dt\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"0.28\", \"1.71x\", \"full differentiation, collapse accelerating\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"双 Y 轴图：左轴 cosine similarity（蓝，下降），右轴 008d normalized v/e（红，上升）。两条曲线交叉区域标注 'critical window: differentiation enables exploitation'。\"\n    analysis: >\n      cosine similarity 分析建立了 dt_embedding training dynamics \n      与 delusional critic onset 的 temporal coupling。\n      这不是相关性而是因果路径上的中间变量：\n      training → embedding differentiation → dt-conditioned value learning \n      → exploitation of RSSM error → collapse。\n      untrained embedding 的恒定 similarity 解释了为什么 protection 是 structural。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_040: Hopper Hop validation (P2, stretch)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: >\n      第三个 DMC 环境验证，强化 generalization claim。\n      3 configs = baseline + trained dt_emb + dt_embed_dim=0。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_asymptotic_mean: 250\n      baseline_asymptotic_std: 30\n      trained_dtEmb_collapse: \"3/3 seeds\"\n      trained_dtEmb_peak_normalized_ve: 1.70\n      no_dtEmb_normalized_ve_55K: 0.80\n      no_dtEmb_eval_55K_vs_baseline_pct: 28\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 是 DMC 中难度较高的环境（DreamerV3 baseline ~200-300），\n      RSSM 对 hopping dynamics 的建模难度更大（contact dynamics, \n      discontinuous state transitions）。因此 dt=2 的 RSSM fidelity gap \n      可能更大 → trained dt_emb 的 collapse 可能更快。\n      但在 best tier 下，同一机制仍然 hold：\n      trained dt_emb → v/e >1.5x → collapse；no dt_emb → v/e <1.0x → stable。\n      有了三个环境的一致结果，论文可以 claim \"the mechanism generalizes \n      across DMC locomotion tasks\"。Hopper Hop 是 P2 stretch goal，\n      不是 blocking，但如果完成，将使 generalization claim 从 \n      \"two environments\" 升级为 \"three diverse environments\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Three-Environment Mechanism Consistency\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Environment\", \"Trained dt_emb collapse\", \"No dt_emb stable\", \"Norm v/e threshold holds\"]\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"3/3 ✓\", \"3/3 ✓\", \"✓ (1.5x)\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run (pred)\", \"3/3 ✓\", \"3/3 ✓\", \"✓ (1.5x)\"]\n          - [\"Hopper Hop (pred)\", \"3/3 ✓\", \"3/3 ✓\", \"✓ (1.5x)\"]\n          - [\"Total\", \"9/9\", \"9/9\", \"100% consistent\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3×2 panel：三行（三个环境），两列（eval return, normalized v/e）。每个 panel 叠加 trained dt_emb（红）和 no dt_emb（蓝）。所有红线 collapse，所有蓝线 stable，视觉上极具冲击力。\"\n    analysis: >\n      三环境 × 多种子 = 论文最强的泛化证据。\n      9/9 collapse + 9/9 stable 的 binary 一致性使得 p-value < 0.001\n      （binomial test），即使不做 formal hypothesis testing，\n      reviewer 也很难质疑机制的 generality。\n      但 Hopper Hop 是 45 GPU-hours，在 deadline 前可能无法完成。\n      即使没有 Hopper Hop，Walker + Cheetah 的 6/6 + 6/6 已经足够。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"bef9a362-8ebf-4bcb-9f30-9fef8cba03ac","total_cost_usd":0.541909,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20446,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":15707,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20446,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15707,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20446,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20446},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":15406,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.015516,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15707,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":20446,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.526393,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"2e61b2ab-2ef5-4d83-9c15-e745ea3f1432"}
